          "message": {
            "text": "Fallback priority is a one-shot iterator stage, not a parameter on ordinary system fallback. Advancing the state to system before returning the priority candidate reproduces Blink’s ownership: a failed/requeued priority face cannot be asked twice, and the next candidate is the platform fallback.",
            "markdown": "Fallback priority is a one-shot iterator stage, not a parameter on ordinary system fallback. Advancing the state to system before returning the priority candidate reproduces Blink’s ownership: a failed/requeued priority face cannot be asked twice, and the next candidate is the platform fallback."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
