          "guid": "msponf5o0yytsnni",
          "message": {
            "text": "Environment invalidation clears shaped-cluster verdicts while ordinary memory trim preserves them. The key names a face by path and collection member, so a host font update can replace bytes without changing the key; retaining the verdict across that transition would be stale, whereas retaining it across a memory-only trim is answer-neutral.",
            "markdown": "Environment invalidation clears shaped-cluster verdicts while ordinary memory trim preserves them. The key names a face by path and collection member, so a host font update can replace bytes without changing the key; retaining the verdict across that transition would be stale, whereas retaining it across a memory-only trim is answer-neutral."
          },
